+	 * Diagnostic: logs failing BSD syscalls of processes whose p_comm contains NAME:
+	 * "SYSERR name[pid] sc N err E a0 a1 a2 'str0' 'str1'" (a0/a1 that point at a readable user string are shown as
+	 * strings). Finds what a daemon trips over when its own log says nothing. NAME from boot-arg sweetsystrace=NAME
+	 * or, at run time (2026-11-23), sysctl kern.sweet_systrace=NAME (empty: off). The everyday misses (ENOENT, ESRCH,
